Found while reviewing examples/monitor.svg for k8 (wall screen, 48 synthetic Combs). A name longer than about 11 characters is cut with an ellipsis, so notification-service-12 and notification-service-28 both read "notificati…" and can only be told apart by the tooltip - which a wall screen does not have. Idea: break a name that does not fit at a hyphen or dot into two lines and cut only what still does not fit. Needs a SPEC decision (§6 says "cut with an ellipsis") - maintainer call. Names that fit today must render byte-identical (demo.svg, monitor.svg unchanged).

Confirmed on the real CitiAI cluster (2026-10-02): at size 56 half of the names are cut - cert-manag…, gpu-operat… - on a page meant for a wall screen without tooltips. Raises the priority.

